  "goodToKnow": "Die Volksgruppe is an ethnic group, especially a minority within a state, a term used in Austria and international law (Volksgruppenrecht). Germany's four recognised national minorities are Danes in Schleswig, Frisians, Sorbs in Lusatia, and German Sinti and Roma; the Sorbs have bilingual road signs. In neutral modern German, people also say ethnische Gruppe or Ethnie. Plural: die Volksgruppen."
